are given. kspacing ( float ) – Generate a grid of k-points with this as the minimum distance,\nin A^-1 between them in reciprocal space. If set to None, kpts\nwill be used instead. kpts ( ( int , int , int ) , dict or np.ndarray ) – If kpts is a tuple (or list) of 3 integers, it is interpreted\nas the dimensions of a Monkhorst-Pack grid. If kpts is set to None , only the Γ-point will be included\nand QE will use routines optimized for Γ-point-only calculations.', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_espresso_in', 'class': None, 'function': 'write_espresso_in', 'chunk_index': 2, 'num_chunks': 5}, 'score': 7.324000358581543, 'vector_score': 0.5066214799880981, 'bm25_score': 23.34422922597874, 'rerank_score': 7.324000358581543}, {'text': "[ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso]\ninput_data: dict A flat or nested dictionary with input parameters for pw.x pseudopotentials: dict A filename for each atomic species, e.g. {'O': 'O.pbe-rrkjus.UPF', 'H': 'H.pbe-rrkjus.UPF'} . A dummy name will be used if none are given. kspacing: float Generate a grid of k-points with this as the minimum distance,\nin A^-1 between them in reciprocal space. If set to None, kpts\nwill be used instead. kpts: (int, int, int), dict, or BandPath If kpts is a tuple (or list) of 3 integers, it is interpreted\nas the dimensions of a Monkhorst-Pack grid. If kpts is set to None , only the Γ-point will be included\nand QE will use routines optimized for Γ-point-only calculations. Compared to Γ-point-only calculations without this optimization\n(i.e. with kpts=(1, 1, 1) ), the memory and CPU requirements\nare typically reduced by half.", 'title': 'ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/calculators/espresso